> How do I open a chest?  Open doesn't work, and kicking it makes the
lid open
> then close...

You *loot* it. If the lid opens and then closes when you kick it, it
is unlocked, and then you use the #loot command to put things into it
or take things out of it.

If the chest is locked, then kicking it can break the lock (but also
risks breaking breakable things inside it: such as potions, eggs, and
items made of glass.) Or, alternatively, you can "a"pply a Key or Lock
Pick if you find such an item - stand on the space containing the
chest, "a"pply the Key or Lock Pick, and then use "." when prompted
for a direction, to investigate the current space. You can then unlock
the chest and #loot it.

> How do I sell to merchants?  I've only gotten down far enough to
meet
> merchants once, but I couldn't figure out how to sell things.  Or
will they
> let me know when they want to buy something?

Drop things on the floors of their shops. If the item is of a type of
item that the merchant will buy, then the merchant will offer you
money for it. If not, he will be uninterested.

But be warned: if you kill a monster in the shop, then ALL of the
monster's items are considered as belonging to the shopkeeper - even
if they're of a type that the shopkeeper doesn't normally sell. For
instance, if you kill a goblin wearing an iron skullcap in a potion
shop, if you pick up the skullcap the shopkeeper will not let you
leave the shop without paying for it. Likewise if you willingly drop
the "wrong" type of item in a shop (in which case the shopkeeper will
seem uninterested), then leave the shop and come back, the shopkeeper
will consider himself the owner of the item.

The FIRST square inside a shop - the one directly in front of the
door - belongs to the player. Any items that land on that square
belong to the player - if your pet picks up an item from elsewhere in
the shop and drops it on the square directly adjacent to the door,
then you have robbed the shop for free. ;-)

